		{
			description: [
				"Epoxy resin is a polymer compound with the structural characteristics of an epoxy group (-O-). It is usually a high-performance thermosetting plastic formed by the reaction of epoxy monomer and curing agent. Epoxy resin has good mechanical properties, electrical insulation properties, chemical stability and bonding properties, and is widely used in coatings, adhesives, electronic packaging, building reinforcement, composite materials and other fields."
				""
				"It is recommended to steam crack naphtha to obtain propylene (of course it would be best if your petrochemical production line is completely built)"
